--- !u!114 &1688354191
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1688354189}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5643c5a6c1771d846840e6723ca78057, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  inGameText1:
  - {fileID: 741986703}
  - {fileID: 1581421024}
  - {fileID: 1426487601}
  - {fileID: 680186012}
  - {fileID: 212297149}
  - {fileID: 1934703928}
  - {fileID: 1514805714}
  - {fileID: 831538646}
  - {fileID: 1864781193}
  - {fileID: 1591572096}
  - {fileID: 309093051}
  - {fileID: 608335534}
  - {fileID: 162945400}
  inGameText2:
  - {fileID: 2077894927}
  - {fileID: 2112879428}
  - {fileID: 424933798}
  - {fileID: 1778409047}
  - {fileID: 250145564}
  - {fileID: 1601546414}
  - {fileID: 1609576835}
  - {fileID: 1568824081}
  - {fileID: 723905386}
  - {fileID: 358490852}
  - {fileID: 926150627}
  - {fileID: 564479026}
  - {fileID: 1708740748}
  - {fileID: 1249801317}
  textbatch1:
  - It was always easier to lie.
  - Camille deserved more than apologies.
  - You promised her a better life.
  - You said you'd always provide.
  - You turned away when it mattered most.
  - You let it happen.
  - You never came home.
  - 'You chose the dice over them. '
  - You told her it was under control.
  - You used to be someone she admired.
  - "Eleanor doesn\u2019t remember your voice."
  - All that charm... wasted on excuses.
  - What did you think would happen?
  - You knew this day would come.
  - It started with one lie.
  textbatch2:
  - "All your riches, and still, you couldn\u2019t protect them."
  - You gambled their safety for wine and wenches.
  - You were too late.
  - "You\u2019re not fighting for them. You\u2019re fighting to feel clean."
  - Even your lies were half-hearted.
  - You sold your soul at the gambling table.
  - "You didn\u2019t steal to save them. You stole to fix your mess."
  - "Eleanor still draws you with a crown. She doesn\u2019t know."
  textbatch3:
  - "They don\u2019t respect you."
  - How many lives did your pride destroy?
  - You let someone else pay the price.
  - "You'll never be enough\u2014not for them, not for yourself."
  - You let the world burn around you.
  - They died waiting for your help.
  - Redemption? It's just another lie you tell yourselves.
  - Too little. Too late.
  - You only made it worse.
  - Verita cannot clean the blood off your hands.
  - You waited too long to change.
  - All this pain. All this ruin. For what?
  - "You weren\u2019t saving them. You were saving yourself."
  - You wanted to be forgiven without confessing.
  textbatch4:
  - You'll never be a real knight.
  - Verita sees through you.
  - You have no will of your own.
  - You are too weak to question.
  - You died for them. And still, he wasn't enough to save you.
  - He'll kill for you. And you won't even be there to stop it.
  - You will die serving a lie.
  - You wear humility to hide your fear.
  - The Order made you. You never chose it.
  - You only follow orders. Never your heart.
  - You tried to make yourself into someone worthy.
  - You passed every trial. Except the one you kept hidden.
  - "You fought so hard to be seen\u2026 and still, they looked right through you."
  - Not even Verita spoke your true name.
